msgid "Now for each matrix we will build up a Krylov subspace and calculate eigenvalues in steps. At each step, we will check to see if the lowest eigenvalue has been obtained to within our specified absolute error. The subspace that first gives us eigenvalues within our specified error is the subspace for which we will record computation times. Executing this cell may take several minutes, depending on processor speed. Feel free to skip evaluation or reduce the maximum dimension of matrices diagonalized. Looking at the pre-calculated results is sufficient.\n"
